My father gave us everything, as much as they could. We were going to camp summertime. We had all the activities, sports. We were going skiing, and ice skating. And even we enjoyed-- went to school for ballet-- dancing. Because my parents believe in diversified education.

Naturally, they did not push us to school, because they knew that we will be good students, and we will grow up, and we know what is right and what is wrong. So I think in all our time, when we were little, we did not need coaching from parents who say, don't do this or don't do that. We were born with the knowledge what was right.

