Naturally, we left everything in the house as it was. We walked out. And we went to live with a family in a Jewish neighborhood.

So we were lucky. Somebody took us in. We were five people, and the lady had also four people. We were 10 people. And then she another two people-- about 12 people in two-room two-- two-room apartment. We slept, like, you know, on the cots, on the floors.

