In spite of this, we heard a-- a lot atrocities which German did in Germany, in '36, I think was it, when they threw out the Polish Jews from Germany. And they used to come and tell stories. We always-- we said, it's impossible how a man can kill another man for no reason whatsoever.

INT: Mm-hmm.

JT: So we were fooled. With the German upbringing and German culture, we were fooled.

